1
00:00:15,260 --> 00:00:16,917
Destiny. Fate. Dreams.

2
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:21,140
These unstoppable ideals are
held deep in the heart of man.

3
00:00:21,560 --> 00:00:24,937
As long as there are people
who seek freedom in this life,

4
00:00:25,020 --> 00:00:27,667
these things shall not
vanish from the earth.

5
00:00:34,720 --> 00:00:37,517
People tell me my head's in the clouds.

6
00:00:37,600 --> 00:00:40,877
I don't care what they say
because I'm dreaming of you.

7
00:00:40,960 --> 00:00:43,557
You are the treasure I found.

8
00:00:43,640 --> 00:00:46,657
So bright, so bold, it's so elusive.

9
00:00:46,740 --> 00:00:48,737
It's hard to look away.

10
00:00:48,820 --> 00:00:51,837
Even though it's blinding me.

11
00:00:51,920 --> 00:00:55,657
There are no words to
describe how I feel inside.

12
00:00:55,740 --> 00:00:58,020
I'm really, really stuck on you.

13
00:00:59,220 --> 00:01:02,537
I have to follow my dreams,
however crazy they seem.

14
00:01:02,620 --> 00:01:05,597
And I won't stop till I
get there, you will see.

15
00:01:05,680 --> 00:01:08,877
You're all I need to have
the strength to believe.

16
00:01:08,960 --> 00:01:12,520
Believe in wonderland.

17
00:01:17,880 --> 00:01:21,097
I'm gonna follow my dreams,
however crazy they seem.

18
00:01:21,180 --> 00:01:24,157
I'm gonna share them
with you, a love so true.

19
00:01:24,240 --> 00:01:27,557
You're all I want,
together we can move on.

20
00:01:27,640 --> 00:01:29,917
We live how we want to.

21
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:32,037
There is no limit to us.

22
00:01:32,120 --> 00:01:33,537
We have the power of love.

23
00:01:33,620 --> 00:01:36,617
We don't want to live ordinary life.

24
00:01:36,700 --> 00:01:39,657
We have a chance to live in paradise.

25
00:01:39,740 --> 00:01:42,520
We believe in one another.

26
00:01:51,160 --> 00:01:54,500
Well, Straw Hat Luffy,
this is a good way to die.

27
00:01:57,960 --> 00:02:02,019
Within six minutes, this yard will
be blown up along with the square.

28
00:02:02,400 --> 00:02:04,106
I'd stay, but I'm in a hurry.

29
00:02:04,540 --> 00:02:06,422
You just wait right there, okay?

30
00:02:07,200 --> 00:02:10,729
And then you can celebrate the
new king of the sand country.

31
00:02:12,920 --> 00:02:13,750
Now then.

32
00:02:17,640 --> 00:02:19,240
I should be on my way.

33
00:02:19,620 --> 00:02:22,914
He said it's in the Mortuary
Temple to the west of here.

34
00:02:31,900 --> 00:02:32,730
Missed me.

35
00:02:43,980 --> 00:02:45,760
That was way too close!

36
00:02:51,480 --> 00:02:52,520
That bastard!

37
00:02:52,760 --> 00:02:53,640
He took off!

38
00:02:54,820 --> 00:02:57,140
I think he flew off in that direction.

39
00:02:57,640 --> 00:02:59,287
He won't get away with this!

40
00:02:59,460 --> 00:03:00,320
Damn him!

41
00:03:11,400 --> 00:03:13,480
So this is the royal tomb,

42
00:03:13,880 --> 00:03:17,292
where generations of your kings
lay in their eternal rest.

43
00:03:18,940 --> 00:03:21,180
So, where's the Poneglyph?

44
00:03:33,920 --> 00:03:35,280
Hidden Stairs

45
00:03:36,040 --> 00:03:39,600
The Poneglyph is kept down
there, deep underground

46
00:03:40,840 --> 00:03:43,677
Most people aren't even aware
of the Poneglyph's existence

47
00:03:43,760 --> 00:03:47,677
Many events occur behind the
scenes Just because a country

48
00:03:47,760 --> 00:03:50,617
belongs to the world government
Doesn't necessarily mean

49
00:03:50,700 --> 00:03:54,300
that its king knows what's
going on You shouldn't be blamed

50
00:03:55,020 --> 00:03:56,140
Like most people,

51
00:03:56,340 --> 00:03:58,557
you probably had no idea
there was someone left

52
00:03:58,640 --> 00:04:00,757
in the world who can
decipher the ancient writing.

53
00:04:00,840 --> 00:04:02,517
You can actually read poneglyphs?

54
00:04:02,600 --> 00:04:03,430
That's right.

55
00:04:03,513 --> 00:04:07,077
That's why Crocodile and I ended
up as a team in the first place.

56
00:04:07,160 --> 00:04:08,757
It's also why he can't kill me.

57
00:04:08,840 --> 00:04:09,781
I'm no use dead.

58
00:04:10,960 --> 00:04:15,537
Tell me, is it correct that the poneglyph
in this country tells where Pluton is?

59
00:04:15,620 --> 00:04:17,032
Is that really the case?

60
00:04:18,560 --> 00:04:22,417
Alabasta's royal family has been obligated
for generations now to protect it.

61
00:04:22,500 --> 00:04:27,720
That duty is about the only thing we
know about it protect don't make me laugh

62
00:04:34,180 --> 00:04:36,237
This place is quite impressive.

63
00:04:36,320 --> 00:04:38,732
It's located behind the doors in the back

64
00:04:47,220 --> 00:04:48,680
There it is

65
00:04:52,940 --> 00:04:53,770
This way!

66
00:04:59,480 --> 00:05:00,820
Now you died!

67
00:05:01,660 --> 00:05:02,778
What are you doing?

68
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:03,830
What am I doing?

69
00:05:03,913 --> 00:05:06,137
I'm trying to get inside
Crocodile's head, that's what!

70
00:05:06,220 --> 00:05:08,637
Like if I were him, where would
I want to shoot a cannon from?

71
00:05:08,720 --> 00:05:09,697
Just keep looking!

72
00:05:09,780 --> 00:05:11,309
We only have five minutes!

73
00:05:11,500 --> 00:05:14,257
Five minutes to go before
a million people all die!

74
00:05:14,340 --> 00:05:15,617
We really need to hurry!

75
00:05:15,700 --> 00:05:18,277
We don't have much time
left to find the cannon!

76
00:05:18,360 --> 00:05:20,697
Chopper, do you think you can
find the guy by using your nose?

77
00:05:20,780 --> 00:05:21,610
That won't work.

78
00:05:21,693 --> 00:05:24,057
The only thing I can smell
anywhere is gunpowder.

79
00:05:24,140 --> 00:05:25,337
We have to do something!

80
00:05:25,420 --> 00:05:28,757
Try finding the smell of a guy who's about
to blow up the square with a big cannon!

81
00:05:28,840 --> 00:05:30,037
What kind of smell is that?

82
00:05:30,120 --> 00:05:30,957
How should I know?

83
00:05:31,040 --> 00:05:31,870
Just try it!

84
00:05:36,600 --> 00:05:39,365
A cannonball that can
blow up that big an area?

85
00:05:40,440 --> 00:05:41,270
Hold on.

86
00:05:41,353 --> 00:05:42,717
In that case, it's gotta be really big.

87
00:05:42,800 --> 00:05:46,217
And if it's gonna be shot out of a
cannon, it surely can't go very far.

88
00:05:46,300 --> 00:05:49,124
So it's gotta be closer
to the square than this!

89
00:05:49,800 --> 00:05:50,630
Ah!

90
00:05:50,713 --> 00:05:52,613
There's no way I have time to go around!

91
00:05:52,720 --> 00:05:53,779
There, a shortcut!

92
00:05:55,820 --> 00:05:57,467
Anything from the sky, Pell?

93
00:05:57,580 --> 00:06:01,277
I searched every rooftop near the square,
but I couldn't see any sign of a cannon.

94
00:06:01,360 --> 00:06:04,184
Well, then, it might be
in a building somewhere.

95
00:06:04,560 --> 00:06:05,857
Right, I'll search them all.

96
00:06:05,940 --> 00:06:06,770
Good!

97
00:06:18,720 --> 00:06:21,780
How many times must you
try this before giving up?

98
00:06:33,200 --> 00:06:34,640
Crocodile, it's you.

99
00:06:36,840 --> 00:06:39,660
Looks like Nico Robin
made short work of you.

100
00:06:39,980 --> 00:06:43,377
I must say, I never thought the
Marines would follow me to the city.

101
00:06:43,460 --> 00:06:44,580
Where's your boss?

102
00:06:44,940 --> 00:06:48,116
Did that smoky idiot run
away and leave you all alone?

103
00:06:48,600 --> 00:06:50,877
Justice is only for
the people who take it.

104
00:06:50,960 --> 00:06:53,431
That's the kind of world we live in, girl.

105
00:06:53,520 --> 00:06:55,637
Why don't you just go back
to your base and talk about

106
00:06:55,720 --> 00:06:58,779
justice until you're actually
ready to fight for it?

107
00:07:09,260 --> 00:07:10,090
Crocodile!

108
00:07:20,160 --> 00:07:24,697
crocodile Straw Hat where'd he go where

109
00:07:24,780 --> 00:07:30,380
tell me right now which way did he go

110
00:07:45,440 --> 00:07:47,980
Towards the temple. That way.

111
00:07:48,400 --> 00:07:50,480
That direction! Thank you!

112
00:08:04,540 --> 00:08:06,800
What justice is there?

113
00:08:12,880 --> 00:08:15,780
To hell with Marine Headquarters.

114
00:08:25,120 --> 00:08:27,520
Jeez, I can't move very well.

115
00:08:28,800 --> 00:08:30,320
This is strange.

116
00:08:30,820 --> 00:08:32,100
I ate all that meat.

117
00:08:33,200 --> 00:08:34,260
What's wrong?

118
00:08:34,400 --> 00:08:35,753
These wounds are small.

119
00:08:36,960 --> 00:08:39,460
I wonder if I should lie down.

120
00:08:42,100 --> 00:08:45,600
Well, did it tell you everything
that you wanted to know?

121
00:08:53,440 --> 00:08:55,340
Now I see it.

122
00:08:55,760 --> 00:08:57,040
Secret stairs.

123
00:09:02,040 --> 00:09:03,780
Just four more minutes!

124
00:09:27,520 --> 00:09:29,317
Aren't there any others around?

125
00:09:29,400 --> 00:09:31,753
Is this all that your country is hiding?

126
00:09:31,940 --> 00:09:33,175
You aren't satisfied?

127
00:09:33,440 --> 00:09:36,499
I have kept every word of
the promise I made to you.

128
00:09:37,620 --> 00:09:38,460
You did.

129
00:09:40,700 --> 00:09:42,940
Just like any other national secret.

130
00:09:43,740 --> 00:09:48,622
No matter how hard you look, you can't find
it unless you already know where it is.

131
00:09:49,660 --> 00:09:52,480
So, this is the Poneglyph
we were looking for.

132
00:09:54,300 --> 00:09:55,697
That didn't take much time.

133
00:09:55,780 --> 00:10:00,427
Now that you have this odd thing in front
of you, were you able to decipher it?

134
00:10:00,820 --> 00:10:02,360
Yes. Very good.

135
00:10:02,700 --> 00:10:03,900
Now, read it aloud.

136
00:10:04,300 --> 00:10:05,771
What does this thing say?

137
00:10:09,340 --> 00:10:11,120
Kahira conquered Alabasta.

138
00:10:11,520 --> 00:10:14,180
In Sky Ephemeris, year 239.

139
00:10:15,480 --> 00:10:18,580
In year 260, Tamer
ruled the Baton dynasty.

140
00:10:19,160 --> 00:10:23,397
In year 306, the Taf Cathedral
was completed in Aramalu.

141
00:10:23,480 --> 00:10:28,560
In year 325, the hero Mamden
of... Hey, hold on! What's this?

142
00:10:28,740 --> 00:10:30,817
Is this really all the information here?

143
00:10:30,900 --> 00:10:33,724
I don't give a damn about
this desert's history.

144
00:10:33,920 --> 00:10:35,737
I want to know about the
world's most dangerous

145
00:10:35,820 --> 00:10:38,277
military power that's
hiding in this country.

146
00:10:38,360 --> 00:10:40,040
Where is the Pluton hidden?

147
00:10:41,280 --> 00:10:43,880
That information isn't on here. What?

148
00:10:44,220 --> 00:10:46,937
History is the only thing
that this text contains.

149
00:10:47,020 --> 00:10:48,540
That's all? Pluton.

150
00:10:48,800 --> 00:10:50,320
I didn't see it anywhere.

151
00:10:50,620 --> 00:10:53,208
It isn't mentioned on
this poneglyph at all.

152
00:10:54,540 --> 00:10:57,200
Not mentioned at all, I see.

153
00:10:57,700 --> 00:10:58,940
That's unfortunate.

154
00:10:59,840 --> 00:11:02,477
You've been an excellent
partner, but even so,

155
00:11:02,560 --> 00:11:05,420
I think that I'll kill you right here.

156
00:11:06,200 --> 00:11:07,030
What?

157
00:11:07,240 --> 00:11:10,828
The agreement that we made four
years ago has been fulfilled.

158
00:11:11,300 --> 00:11:13,888
Do you remember the
terms of that agreement?

159
00:11:14,260 --> 00:11:17,340
I was to bring you to the
Poneglyph, and in turn,

160
00:11:17,620 --> 00:11:20,914
you would hand over the
information on the weapon to me.

161
00:11:21,080 --> 00:11:24,457
The work you've done for Baroque
Works these past four years was

162
00:11:24,540 --> 00:11:28,364
excellent both in terms of intellect
and your ability to command.

163
00:11:28,500 --> 00:11:32,637
Your usefulness to the company has
been reason enough to keep you around.

164
00:11:32,720 --> 00:11:35,180
But in the end, you've spoiled it all.

165
00:11:35,420 --> 00:11:37,980
By betraying me, Nico Robin!

166
00:11:40,940 --> 00:11:45,587
You say the poneglyph in this country
doesn't say anything at all about Pluton.

167
00:11:45,800 --> 00:11:46,940
Is that true? You?

168
00:11:47,420 --> 00:11:50,597
Was this the plan all along to
hide the information from me,

169
00:11:50,680 --> 00:11:53,445
even if you were able to
find something useful?

170
00:11:57,620 --> 00:12:01,260
But even so, I don't feel
any anger toward you.

171
00:12:01,460 --> 00:12:03,900
And do you know why that is, Nico Robin?

172
00:12:04,900 --> 00:12:05,920
Huh. All right.

173
00:12:06,120 --> 00:12:07,817
I've worked with you for four years.

174
00:12:07,900 --> 00:12:11,797
I knew you'd try something like this
someday, so I'm more than ready.

175
00:12:11,880 --> 00:12:12,710
One!

176
00:12:13,140 --> 00:12:16,316
If you get wet, then a knife
should go right into you!

177
00:12:17,780 --> 00:12:19,300
Damn it! Where'd he go?

178
00:12:24,860 --> 00:12:27,640
Now all is forgiven, Nico Robin.

179
00:12:35,220 --> 00:12:39,396
Because I never trusted you from the
very beginning of our partnership.

180
00:12:39,740 --> 00:12:42,916
I knew better than to do
something as foolish as that.

181
00:12:47,300 --> 00:12:51,320
I can tell from Cobra's reaction
that Pluton really does exist.

182
00:12:51,980 --> 00:12:53,680
I don't need the Poneglyph.

183
00:12:53,820 --> 00:12:55,702
I can find the Pluton on my own.

184
00:12:55,840 --> 00:12:59,016
Once this country is mine,
it's only a matter of time.

185
00:13:01,320 --> 00:13:02,197
What's happening?

186
00:13:02,280 --> 00:13:05,221
It's still too early for
the attack on the square.

187
00:13:05,680 --> 00:13:07,600
It must be you. What did you do?

188
00:13:08,560 --> 00:13:09,857
It's just a little present.

189
00:13:09,940 --> 00:13:11,040
You see,

190
00:13:11,260 --> 00:13:14,637
this underground temple was built so
that disturbing just one small column

191
00:13:14,720 --> 00:13:18,477
will destroy the balance of the entire
structure and cause it to collapse.

192
00:13:18,560 --> 00:13:20,736
The two of you are going to die here.

193
00:13:20,880 --> 00:13:22,409
We'll meet death together.

194
00:13:23,400 --> 00:13:26,700
I am the Twelfth King
of the Nefertari family.

195
00:13:26,840 --> 00:13:27,877
I will uphold our honor.

196
00:13:27,960 --> 00:13:31,784
Someone like you can never be
allowed to rule the Desert Kingdom.

197
00:13:35,420 --> 00:13:36,250
Impressive.

198
00:13:36,333 --> 00:13:40,528
You truly are a model king, willing to
give your own life just to take me down

199
00:13:42,280 --> 00:13:44,057
with you for your kingdom.

200
00:13:44,140 --> 00:13:46,237
Except I won't die.

201
00:13:46,320 --> 00:13:48,908
All I have to do is
change the rocks to sand

202
00:13:51,000 --> 00:13:52,297
and I can escape from here.

203
00:13:52,380 --> 00:13:54,257
Your death will be in vain, Cobra.

204
00:13:54,340 --> 00:13:58,017
There are only three
minutes Left when the square

205
00:13:58,100 --> 00:14:00,997
blows up and this temple
collapses everyone standing

206
00:14:01,080 --> 00:14:04,537
in my way will be eliminated
in an instant and in

207
00:14:04,620 --> 00:14:08,160
that moment this land
will become mine entirely?

208
00:14:30,960 --> 00:14:34,997
Three minutes left
where is it a cannon big

209
00:14:35,080 --> 00:14:37,177
enough to destroy such
a large area has to be

210
00:14:37,260 --> 00:14:40,017
enormous there can't be
many places to hide such

211
00:14:40,100 --> 00:14:43,197
a weapon so why are we
still unable to find it?

212
00:14:43,280 --> 00:14:47,640
But after all this, open space
where a cannon would fit.

213
00:14:48,280 --> 00:14:49,200
Stop shooting!

214
00:14:51,000 --> 00:14:51,960
Open space.

215
00:14:54,200 --> 00:14:55,520
That's not fair, Koza.

216
00:14:55,720 --> 00:14:57,937
Hiding in a place like
this the entire time?

217
00:14:58,020 --> 00:14:59,314
Yeah, leader, no fair!

218
00:15:00,440 --> 00:15:02,440
Yes, that place would work.

219
00:15:03,080 --> 00:15:03,910
That's dangerous!

220
00:15:03,993 --> 00:15:05,717
I told you to stop shooting at me!

221
00:15:05,800 --> 00:15:06,630
Hey, smoke shark!

222
00:15:06,713 --> 00:15:07,543
It's perfect.

223
00:15:07,840 --> 00:15:09,117
It's hidden and it's big.

224
00:15:09,200 --> 00:15:10,030
Stop it, idiot!

225
00:15:10,113 --> 00:15:11,877
I told you I'm not from the Rebel Army!

226
00:15:11,960 --> 00:15:16,520
Hey, Usopp hammer, Usopp
rubber, that's your teacher.

227
00:15:17,440 --> 00:15:19,557
Do they know who they're
dealing with here?

228
00:15:19,640 --> 00:15:21,197
Don't be afraid when I tell you this.

229
00:15:21,280 --> 00:15:22,110
No, be very afraid.

230
00:15:22,193 --> 00:15:24,160
I am the incredible Captain Usopp.

231
00:15:25,580 --> 00:15:26,410
What?

232
00:15:26,493 --> 00:15:27,323
Oh, it's you, Vivi.

233
00:15:27,406 --> 00:15:28,477
So were you able to find the cannon here?

234
00:15:28,560 --> 00:15:29,390
I know now.

235
00:15:29,473 --> 00:15:30,640
I figured it out. What?

236
00:15:30,760 --> 00:15:31,642
You know where?

237
00:15:32,660 --> 00:15:33,490
There it is.

238
00:15:34,020 --> 00:15:35,797
I'll go ahead and signal everyone.

239
00:15:35,880 --> 00:15:37,645
You're sure about this, right?

240
00:15:38,260 --> 00:15:39,142
Special attack.

241
00:15:39,960 --> 00:15:40,840
Red surface.

242
00:16:10,840 --> 00:16:11,670
Let's go!

243
00:16:19,080 --> 00:16:20,820
I slept good. Wait.

244
00:16:21,180 --> 00:16:22,157
Oh, that's right.

245
00:16:22,240 --> 00:16:23,497
I couldn't move all of a sudden,

246
00:16:23,580 --> 00:16:25,637
so I decided to risk
it and take a nap right

247
00:16:25,720 --> 00:16:28,308
here since there was
really no other choice.

248
00:16:30,780 --> 00:16:33,440
Yeah, and I feel better now. So...

249
00:16:34,500 --> 00:16:37,020
Time for me to beat up Crocodile!

250
00:16:45,380 --> 00:16:48,160
That hole over there looks kind of...

251
00:16:51,120 --> 00:16:52,800
kind of crockish.

252
00:16:54,560 --> 00:16:57,180
It's with this freaky place anyway.

253
00:16:58,080 --> 00:17:00,740
The whole thing is crumbling into pieces.

254
00:17:11,560 --> 00:17:12,740
I'm certain of it.

255
00:17:13,240 --> 00:17:14,777
The cannon has to be in there.

256
00:17:14,860 --> 00:17:17,417
I can't think of any other
options besides that place.

257
00:17:17,500 --> 00:17:20,357
What makes you so sure that
it's in there anyway, Phoebe?

258
00:17:20,440 --> 00:17:23,737
We have to assume that this
dust devil is part of the plan.

259
00:17:23,820 --> 00:17:25,397
The cannon must be in a place where they

260
00:17:25,480 --> 00:17:28,068
can still see well
enough to hit the target.

261
00:17:31,140 --> 00:17:31,970
Also,

262
00:17:32,053 --> 00:17:34,197
it has to be in an open
space where a cannon can fit,

263
00:17:34,280 --> 00:17:36,557
but where it can't be seen from the sky.

264
00:17:36,640 --> 00:17:38,699
This place is big enough, isn't it?

265
00:17:39,540 --> 00:17:42,737
So then let's make it the clan's
secret base, what do you say?

266
00:17:42,820 --> 00:17:43,650
Yeah!

267
00:17:43,920 --> 00:17:45,260
So that has to be it.

268
00:17:45,380 --> 00:17:46,857
It makes perfect sense to me.

269
00:17:46,940 --> 00:17:47,770
Okay, hold on.

270
00:17:47,920 --> 00:17:50,297
We'll leave the others a message
since you're headed this way.

271
00:17:50,380 --> 00:17:51,210
Thanks, Usopp.

272
00:17:51,293 --> 00:17:52,846
I'm going ahead to the tower.

273
00:17:53,420 --> 00:17:54,250
Hey!

274
00:17:54,333 --> 00:17:56,160
Wait, Vivi! Wait! Hurry! Right?

275
00:17:56,700 --> 00:17:57,860
Well, look at that!

276
00:17:58,080 --> 00:17:59,139
It's the princess!

277
00:17:59,340 --> 00:18:00,460
We found her, boys!

278
00:18:02,120 --> 00:18:05,597
Yeah, that was just too easy,
the signal led us right to her.

279
00:18:05,680 --> 00:18:08,777
There are more members of
the Baroque Works Billions.

280
00:18:08,860 --> 00:18:09,690
Oh, no!

281
00:18:10,040 --> 00:18:11,569
We signaled the enemy too!

282
00:18:12,700 --> 00:18:15,517
That smoke, Zuzab's signal,
he must have found it.

283
00:18:15,600 --> 00:18:17,980
Okay, but why is the palace so far away?

284
00:18:19,940 --> 00:18:21,646
Good, it's not far from here.

285
00:18:21,760 --> 00:18:24,637
I wonder if that signal means
that they found the cannoneer.

286
00:18:24,720 --> 00:18:26,191
They must have, let's go!

287
00:18:27,980 --> 00:18:28,810
No!

288
00:18:29,480 --> 00:18:30,310
No!

289
00:18:30,393 --> 00:18:31,660
Noisy attack!

290
00:18:40,400 --> 00:18:42,257
Trimble at the power of my nails!

291
00:18:42,340 --> 00:18:43,752
Come on, baby, let's go.

292
00:18:44,620 --> 00:18:46,320
Hey, over there! Get him!

293
00:19:08,460 --> 00:19:09,577
So it's you?

294
00:19:09,660 --> 00:19:11,857
You can't get away.

295
00:19:11,940 --> 00:19:13,117
You're mine.

296
00:19:13,200 --> 00:19:16,397
How are you still alive?

297
00:19:16,480 --> 00:19:20,757
No matter how many times I kill you,
you just keep coming back for more.

298
00:19:20,840 --> 00:19:23,377
Well, answer me, brat.

299
00:19:23,460 --> 00:19:24,697
How'd he do it?

300
00:19:24,780 --> 00:19:29,260
How did he If you live and
come here, who is this boy?

301
00:19:36,020 --> 00:19:37,060
It's Tryhat.

302
00:19:40,540 --> 00:19:43,364
Tell me, just how many
times do you have to die?

303
00:19:43,600 --> 00:19:46,237
There's something you still
need to return, Crocodile,

304
00:19:46,320 --> 00:19:48,144
and I came here to get it back.

305
00:19:48,680 --> 00:19:50,400
What is this thing I took?

306
00:19:53,280 --> 00:19:54,437
Is it money?

307
00:19:54,520 --> 00:19:55,577
Is it fame?

308
00:19:55,660 --> 00:19:57,177
Or people's trust?

309
00:19:57,260 --> 00:19:58,317
Their lives?

310
00:19:58,400 --> 00:19:59,380
Is it rain?

311
00:20:03,620 --> 00:20:05,660
I have taken all of those things.

312
00:20:05,940 --> 00:20:09,234
So which is it that you want
me to give back, Straw Hat?

313
00:20:09,420 --> 00:20:10,400
This land.

314
00:20:11,380 --> 00:20:12,320
The land?

315
00:20:12,600 --> 00:20:14,857
Really, you should know
better than that by now.

316
00:20:14,940 --> 00:20:17,657
I have no intention of
relinquishing this country.

317
00:20:17,740 --> 00:20:21,780
Why would I, when I'm going to
become its next king before long?

318
00:20:22,840 --> 00:20:25,497
We came to this island
to save Vivi's country,

319
00:20:25,580 --> 00:20:27,933
but then, when we got here, it was gone.

320
00:20:28,300 --> 00:20:29,860
You stole her country!

321
00:20:34,200 --> 00:20:36,320
I have to get to the rebel army.

322
00:20:36,640 --> 00:20:40,700
I must persuade their leader to stop
all of this pointless bloodshed.

323
00:20:41,580 --> 00:20:43,397
Up until a few short years ago,

324
00:20:43,480 --> 00:20:47,715
it was a thriving city full of gardens
and palm trees and lush greenery.

325
00:20:50,300 --> 00:20:55,320
Please, Vivi, you have to stop these
fools from tearing our country apart.

326
00:20:56,460 --> 00:20:59,931
This is her country, and I'm
here to take it back from you.

327
00:21:00,480 --> 00:21:02,127
Then what's wrong with that?

328
00:21:02,460 --> 00:21:05,517
What's so very wrong about
not wanting to see people die?

329
00:21:05,600 --> 00:21:10,129
Just being in this country one day and
taking a look around, even I can tell.

330
00:21:11,840 --> 00:21:14,369
What this country needs
more than anything!

331
00:21:15,500 --> 00:21:17,857
You think that putting
just your life on the

332
00:21:17,940 --> 00:21:20,137
line is enough to stop
this from happening?

333
00:21:20,220 --> 00:21:21,220
What do you mean?

334
00:21:23,620 --> 00:21:26,317
I don't have anything else
I can put on the line.

335
00:21:26,400 --> 00:21:27,740
Just me.

336
00:21:29,780 --> 00:21:33,657
Well, you can at least try putting
all of our lives on the line together!

337
00:21:33,740 --> 00:21:35,220
Aren't we friends, huh?

338
00:21:41,440 --> 00:21:42,720
I will defeat you.

339
00:21:42,920 --> 00:21:44,957
Take this country out of your evil hands.

340
00:21:45,040 --> 00:21:47,700
And then, Vivi will smile again.

341
00:21:50,800 --> 00:21:52,557
Threaten me as much as you like.

342
00:21:52,640 --> 00:21:54,960
But without any water, you're nothing.

343
00:22:05,880 --> 00:22:07,180
This is impossible.

344
00:22:07,620 --> 00:22:10,800
He doesn't have any water,
so how can he kick me?

345
00:22:15,220 --> 00:22:16,817
This is your fault, you monster!

346
00:22:16,900 --> 00:22:20,018
This country would be peaceful
if it weren't for you!

347
00:22:21,320 --> 00:22:22,957
It's heartbreaking, isn't it?

348
00:22:23,040 --> 00:22:27,320
Their love for their kingdom
will be what destroys it.

349
00:22:51,220 --> 00:22:55,380
I see you're using your blood.

350
00:22:57,460 --> 00:22:58,290
Clever.

351
00:23:00,060 --> 00:23:02,540
Blood can harden sand too, can't it?

352
00:23:13,520 --> 00:23:18,660
First rain base, and then the royal
palace, and now, this underground temple.

353
00:23:20,840 --> 00:23:24,460
You should be rewarded for your
insistence on challenging me.

354
00:23:24,700 --> 00:23:28,759
Even after I've put you through hell
twice now, you keep coming back.

355
00:23:32,960 --> 00:23:34,900
You're a pirate, Straw Hat.

356
00:23:35,980 --> 00:23:40,597
You've certainly proven that in your
determination to defeat me, no matter the cost.

357
00:23:40,680 --> 00:23:42,997
And I'll admit that you've
become an annoyingly

358
00:23:43,080 --> 00:23:45,904
persistent opponent during
our three encounters.

359
00:23:46,300 --> 00:23:47,130
Alright.

360
00:23:47,380 --> 00:23:48,260
What's that?

361
00:23:49,580 --> 00:23:51,200
A poisonous hook.

362
00:23:51,580 --> 00:23:52,500
I see.

363
00:23:52,820 --> 00:23:55,467
You seem to be a competent
pirate, I suppose.

364
00:23:55,880 --> 00:23:58,757
So surely you must understand
that a duel between

365
00:23:58,840 --> 00:24:02,193
pirates is always about two
people fighting for survival.

366
00:24:02,640 --> 00:24:06,464
And when that's the case, there's
no such thing as playing dirty.

367
00:24:13,060 --> 00:24:15,480
When the explosion happens in the square,

368
00:24:15,800 --> 00:24:18,388
this place will most
likely crumble to dust.

369
00:24:18,560 --> 00:24:20,480
This will be our final battle.

370
00:24:20,740 --> 00:24:22,980
So let's settle this once and for all.

371
00:24:26,480 --> 00:24:29,304
Smoke was coming from
this direction, wasn't it?

372
00:24:31,260 --> 00:24:32,120
Or was it?

373
00:24:35,220 --> 00:24:37,180
What? The Marines? Hey, look!

374
00:24:37,340 --> 00:24:38,437
It's Roro Noa Saru!

375
00:24:38,520 --> 00:24:39,350
Just great.

376
00:24:39,433 --> 00:24:41,477
I didn't realize the Marines
were in this town now.

377
00:24:41,560 --> 00:24:43,148
I don't have time for this.

378
00:24:43,820 --> 00:24:44,680
Oh, damn it.

379
00:24:44,800 --> 00:24:47,237
I guess I have no choice but
to deal with them quickly.

380
00:24:47,320 --> 00:24:49,477
Why are you here in the
middle of the battlefield?

381
00:24:49,560 --> 00:24:51,137
Yeah, what do you think you're doing here?

382
00:24:51,220 --> 00:24:53,477
Well, I could say the same thing to you.

383
00:24:53,560 --> 00:24:54,390
Hold it, Zoro!

384
00:24:54,680 --> 00:24:55,620
Go that way.

385
00:24:55,800 --> 00:24:58,777
If you head north at the next corner,
then you can reach the Palace Square.

386
00:24:58,860 --> 00:25:00,260
Go back and turn right.

387
00:25:00,460 --> 00:25:01,297
It's not this way.

388
00:25:01,380 --> 00:25:04,960
Are you that stupid?
Stupid. Get out of here! Go!

389
00:25:05,680 --> 00:25:06,557
What the...

390
00:25:06,640 --> 00:25:07,777
How it just...

391
00:25:07,860 --> 00:25:09,389
We have to run faster, BB!

392
00:25:10,040 --> 00:25:11,777
I don't think I can, or something!

393
00:25:11,860 --> 00:25:13,097
Don't let the princess get away!

394
00:25:13,180 --> 00:25:14,577
Our promotions are on the...

395
00:25:14,660 --> 00:25:15,490
Ah!

396
00:25:16,000 --> 00:25:17,020
Ah! Ah!

397
00:25:17,680 --> 00:25:18,510
Ah!

398
00:25:18,593 --> 00:25:19,423
Ah! Ah! Ah! Ah!

399
00:25:20,160 --> 00:25:29,803
Ah!

400
00:25:31,600 --> 00:25:32,620
Uh, thank you.

401
00:25:33,140 --> 00:25:35,140
We're here to help you, not fight.

402
00:25:35,280 --> 00:25:37,697
Go stop the explosion in the square, okay?

403
00:25:37,780 --> 00:25:38,820
Now go, quickly.

404
00:25:38,960 --> 00:25:40,237
Let's get going, Usopp.

405
00:25:40,320 --> 00:25:41,150
Come on, hurry.

406
00:25:41,233 --> 00:25:42,200
Right. Thank you.

407
00:25:56,460 --> 00:25:58,140
Hurry, we have to hurry.

408
00:25:58,560 --> 00:26:00,148
We've wasted a lot of time.

409
00:26:00,320 --> 00:26:02,077
I don't know why they
helped us back there,

410
00:26:02,160 --> 00:26:05,866
but if it weren't for the Marines,
we'd be a lot worse off now.

411
00:26:15,480 --> 00:26:17,000
No, don't look at that.

412
00:26:17,420 --> 00:26:18,937
We don't have time to help them.

413
00:26:19,020 --> 00:26:22,797
If we don't stop the explosion, the
casualties would be a lot worse than that.

414
00:26:22,880 --> 00:26:23,710
Right.

415
00:26:23,840 --> 00:26:27,487
Crying about it isn't going to
stop the attack from happening.

416
00:26:31,140 --> 00:26:34,337
In two minutes, we're either going
to beat them or we're going to die.

417
00:26:34,420 --> 00:26:36,180
We still have time left. Yes.

418
00:26:36,620 --> 00:26:38,580
And we're all helping you. Yes.

419
00:26:43,940 --> 00:26:44,770
Right there.

420
00:26:45,300 --> 00:26:46,500
Phoebe, who's up?

421
00:26:47,300 --> 00:26:48,760
It's Nami and Tony.

422
00:26:49,820 --> 00:26:50,880
What's going on?

423
00:26:51,020 --> 00:26:52,857
The Marines just helped us out back there.

424
00:26:52,940 --> 00:26:54,797
Were you able to find where the cannon is?

425
00:26:54,880 --> 00:26:58,377
We haven't confirmed it yet, but
this is the only place it can be.

426
00:26:58,460 --> 00:27:01,217
We must have passed it a bunch
of times before I realized it.

427
00:27:01,300 --> 00:27:02,653
The cannon is up there.

428
00:27:02,780 --> 00:27:04,545
I'm absolutely sure of it now.

429
00:27:09,960 --> 00:27:12,100
The clock tower? I see.

430
00:27:12,460 --> 00:27:15,077
From up there, he can get a
really good shot at the square.

431
00:27:15,160 --> 00:27:16,917
We still need Pel to get here, though.

432
00:27:17,000 --> 00:27:18,706
It's the only way to stop it.

433
00:27:19,440 --> 00:27:20,270
Pel.

434
00:27:29,440 --> 00:27:30,920
We don't have much time.

435
00:27:32,240 --> 00:27:36,769
I could have sworn I saw the smoke coming
up from somewhere around this area.

436
00:27:37,780 --> 00:27:39,437
Robot, Robot, Robot, Robot.

437
00:27:39,520 --> 00:27:40,700
Did you see that?

438
00:27:40,880 --> 00:27:44,237
I just shot down that big
bird with my Robot, Robot gun.

439
00:27:44,320 --> 00:27:45,660
Quite impressive, huh?

440
00:27:50,700 --> 00:27:51,580
I'm sorry.

441
00:28:12,900 --> 00:28:14,300
Ohhhhhhhhhh

442
00:28:16,620 --> 00:28:17,500
Hair!

443
00:28:19,440 --> 00:28:20,840
Hiyori!

444
00:28:39,840 --> 00:28:41,500
Come on, Pistol!

445
00:29:01,000 --> 00:29:02,680
Oh, my God.

446
00:29:44,320 --> 00:29:45,577
He's so strong.

447
00:29:45,660 --> 00:29:47,013
Who in the world is he?

448
00:29:47,700 --> 00:29:50,817
Crocodile made even our best
warriors look like children.

449
00:29:50,900 --> 00:29:52,980
But now he's actually struggling.

450
00:30:00,500 --> 00:30:04,260
You were skewered, buried
alive, and dried up.

451
00:30:06,160 --> 00:30:10,925
You may have made it through all that,
but you won't escape this time, Straw Hat.

452
00:30:11,080 --> 00:30:12,800
There's no hope for survival.

453
00:30:13,180 --> 00:30:14,180
The game is over.

454
00:30:14,760 --> 00:30:17,172
This poison will spread through you soon.

455
00:30:17,780 --> 00:30:20,680
You know, crocodile, you
just don't understand.

456
00:30:22,720 --> 00:30:24,140
I wonder what happened.

457
00:30:26,140 --> 00:30:28,493
Well, I don't see him up there anywhere.

458
00:30:29,880 --> 00:30:32,337
But I don't think there's
any way we can get to the

459
00:30:32,420 --> 00:30:34,657
top of the tower in less than
a minute without any help?

460
00:30:34,740 --> 00:30:35,916
Well, where are you?

461
00:30:36,060 --> 00:30:36,890
Hurry,

462
00:30:36,973 --> 00:30:38,757
we need you But now we're
going to have to get moving

463
00:30:38,840 --> 00:30:41,497
without him We're gonna have
to climb all these stairs,

464
00:30:41,580 --> 00:30:42,462
you guys ready?

465
00:30:43,000 --> 00:30:43,830
Hey!

466
00:30:43,913 --> 00:30:44,743
Huh?

467
00:30:44,826 --> 00:30:45,656
Nami!

468
00:30:46,000 --> 00:30:46,880
Hey, Vivi!

469
00:30:47,720 --> 00:30:49,977
Sanji, what are you doing
all the way up there?

470
00:30:50,060 --> 00:30:51,119
What do you think?

471
00:30:51,220 --> 00:30:54,220
You left a message where
the smoke was, didn't you?

472
00:30:54,560 --> 00:30:56,777
The message said go to the clock tower,

473
00:30:56,860 --> 00:30:59,077
so I figured I'd better
head up here to meet you.

474
00:30:59,160 --> 00:31:00,336
So what should I do?

475
00:31:00,760 --> 00:31:03,060
Where's the cannoneer, anyway? The top!

476
00:31:03,300 --> 00:31:04,260
He's at the top!

477
00:31:04,500 --> 00:31:06,559
Go up from there and take him down!

478
00:31:07,560 --> 00:31:08,390
Sanji?

479
00:31:09,180 --> 00:31:13,300
Hey, where were you? I was
looking! Zoro? You're here, too?

480
00:31:13,600 --> 00:31:15,365
What are you doing down there?

481
00:31:15,520 --> 00:31:17,657
Funny, I was gonna ask you the same thing!

482
00:31:17,740 --> 00:31:18,570
It was the Marines!

483
00:31:18,653 --> 00:31:20,540
I kept saying, go north, go north!

484
00:31:20,640 --> 00:31:23,177
So I just kept going north
till I got all the way up here!

485
00:31:23,260 --> 00:31:25,460
North and up aren't the same thing!

486
00:31:25,660 --> 00:31:27,260
Anyway, good job, you two!

487
00:31:27,560 --> 00:31:30,877
Now just keep on going up from there
and destroy the clock tower, okay?

488
00:31:30,960 --> 00:31:31,790
No way!

489
00:31:32,240 --> 00:31:35,397
They can't get inside the clock
tower from where they are now.

490
00:31:35,480 --> 00:31:37,537
You see, there are only two ways in.

491
00:31:37,620 --> 00:31:40,157
The back stairs on the first
floor and from the sky.

492
00:31:40,240 --> 00:31:41,652
That's why we need Pell!

493
00:31:41,780 --> 00:31:44,457
But can't Zoro just go ahead and
destroy the wall or something?

494
00:31:44,540 --> 00:31:45,517
We can't risk that.

495
00:31:45,600 --> 00:31:48,557
It could make the cannonball explode
even earlier for all we know.

496
00:31:48,640 --> 00:31:50,857
We have no choice but to take the stairs.

497
00:31:50,940 --> 00:31:52,200
No, wait, Vivi!

498
00:31:53,260 --> 00:31:55,060
I think I have a better plan!

499
00:32:10,620 --> 00:32:12,140
So, Mr. Seven,

500
00:32:12,400 --> 00:32:14,237
according to what the boss told us,

501
00:32:14,320 --> 00:32:17,317
this is going to be our final
mission for Baroque Works!

502
00:32:17,400 --> 00:32:18,230
Robot!

503
00:32:18,313 --> 00:32:19,143
Robot!

504
00:32:19,226 --> 00:32:20,056
Robot!

505
00:32:20,500 --> 00:32:22,382
That's right, Miss Father's Day!

506
00:32:24,280 --> 00:32:27,692
According to the plan, we have
just 30 seconds left to go.

507
00:32:29,800 --> 00:32:31,900
Who are they? Mr.

508
00:32:32,220 --> 00:32:34,660
Seven and Miss Father's Day.
